Anime-style wide illustration, clean line art, soft cel shading, gentle natural colours, cinematic composition, no text, no letters, no readable marks. Entirely underwater, a vision of the sea as it was long ago: clean bright clear water full of golden light and life, never dark. Slender lit towers of a lost city of the ancient builders glow warmly from within, and between the towers a few children of about six to ten years old swim, bare-limbed, wearing only plain pale cloth wraps, mixed light and brown skin, hair floating, happy, eyes with irises and highlights; no uniforms, no neckties, no babies. Behind them unbroken kelp forests run away to the distance. High above glides the young Dragon seen from the side: a kilometre of new pale metal ribs, each rib a great hoop, one behind another in a long sinuous line, with bright glowing water bound to the ribs streaming back like a flame from a torch; its head is a smooth blunt rounded pale prow with absolutely no eyes, no mouth, no face, no fins, no wings. A web of bright glowing roads leads away from it over the sea floor. No sky, no horizon.
